\newpage
\begin{description}
\item[* name:] TPPSNegAdapt
\item[* relevant examples:] \mbox{}\\
1. Not to somebody could I tell my story $\rightarrow$ To nobody could I tell 
my story\\
2. Not to someone could I tell my story $\rightarrow$ To noone could I tell 
my story\\
3. Not with something on my mind I left the house $\rightarrow$ With nothing on 
my mind I left the house\\
4. ?Not to somewhere in particular did they bring me $\rightarrow$ To nowhere 
in particular did they bring me (is inversion needed?)
\item[* language:] (Dutch, English, Spanish) English
\item[* kind of rule:] (M-rule, S-rule, Transferrule) M-rule
\item[* subgrammar:] ClauseToSentence
\item[* class:] (name of rule, transformation or filter class) TC\_
NegAdaptation
\item[* date of creation:] 22-SEP-1988 
\item[* author:] margreet sanders
\item[* copied from:] Dutch TNegadapt3
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: 06/03/89\ \ \ \ \ author: margreet sanders.\\
The attributes {\em req\/} and {\em env\/} should not be copied to the higher 
record, since they are dealt with by a special polarity function in RUtt...
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] To let the word {\em not\/} melt with the object of an 
immediately following prepobj in the S, if the object allows it.
\item[\ \ strategy:] (also: deviations from accepted proposals)
\item[\ \ rejected alternatives:]
\item[\ \ clarification of variables:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the splitting up into subrules:] one subrule for 
every word; no examples of melting with `ever' in a prepp could be found
\item[\ \ clarification of the collapsing of rules:] (e.g. clarification of parameters)
\item[\ \ differences analytical/generative version:] this rule only works in 
analysis; it is assumed that in generation other ways will be found to spell 
out the negation
\item[\  \ suggested semantics:]
\item[\ \ presuppositions:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item dictionary:\\

\item rules:\\

\end{enumerate}
